        "ggB-HUfPqOn_text": "<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Here's where things get interesting.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Many busy men already have a morning routine.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Coffee.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Maybe two cups.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Maybe three.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">It's how they get themselves moving.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">And there's nothing inherently wrong with enjoying coffee.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Caffeine can improve alertness and help you feel more awake.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">But feeling awake and being well-rested aren't the same thing.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">If you're sleeping five hours a night, another cup of coffee doesn't replace the sleep you missed.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">If you're constantly stressed, caffeine doesn't resolve the source of that stress.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">And if you're experiencing a persistent change in sexual desire, coffee alone isn't a treatment.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">For some people, consuming too much caffeine—especially later in the day—can also interfere with sleep.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">So instead of thinking about coffee as the answer to everything, it may be more useful to think about your entire daily routine.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Your sleep.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Your physical activity.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Your nutrition.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Your stress.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">And the habits you repeat every morning.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Because these are all parts of the bigger picture.</span></p>",
