        "ggPEaFNaoCO_text": "<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">When men notice changes in their sex drive, testosterone is often one of the first things they think about.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">And understandably so.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Testosterone plays an important role in male sexual desire.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Some men discover that their levels are low and work with a doctor to address it.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Others get tested and find something confusing.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Their testosterone is normal.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Yet their desire still isn't what it used to be.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">So what now?</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">They start searching for answers.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Maybe it's their weight.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Maybe it's stress.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Maybe they need to exercise more.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Maybe they just need to accept that they're getting older.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Some start looking at testosterone supplements.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Others try changing their diet, going back to the gym, or cutting out alcohol.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Those changes can be worthwhile.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">But they don't explain every case.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">And here's something important that often gets overlooked:</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Low sexual desire and difficulty getting an erection aren't necessarily the same problem.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">A man can want sex and still have trouble maintaining an erection.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Another man can have normal erectile function but rarely feel interested in sex.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Understanding that distinction matters because the possible causes—and the appropriate ways to address them—can be different.</span></p>",
